      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:list:parameters:0010:0002",
      "source": "`B`: The right-hand sides `B` to solve for. If `A` has dimension `m x n`, then `B` must have dimension `m x nrhs`, where nrhs is the number of right-hand sides to find solutions for.",
      "ko": "`B`: The right-hand sides `B` to solve for. If `A` has dimension `m x n`, then `B` must have dimension `m x nrhs`, where nrhs is the number of right-hand sides to find solutions for.",
      "sourceHash": "50043d3e8f99485fbf9d655f49ef08476d3144134d60d920b0e0354c62afc2b2",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:list:parameters:0010:0003",
      "source": "`X`: Matrix in which to return solutions. If `A` has dimension `m x n`, and `B` has dimension `m x nrhs`, then `X` must have dimension `n x nrhs`.",
      "ko": "`X`: Matrix in which to return solutions. If `A` has dimension `m x n`, and `B` has dimension `m x nrhs`, then `X` must have dimension `n x nrhs`.",
